Subject: [PATCH] drm/bridge: lt9611: retry transient arbitration loss on power-on

Build685 exposed -EAGAIN from the initial power-on sequence. A later connector
reprobe without reset or rebind retrieved valid EDID with no transfer errors.
The pinned i.MX I2C adapter leaves retries at its zero-initialised default.

Retry the idempotent power-on configuration sequence only for -EAGAIN, up to
three total attempts with 1-2 ms backoff after a retryable failure. Preserve
immediate failure for permanent errors and power_on=false on exhaustion.
Log successful recovery. This is not a blind startup sleep or rebind service;
cold/warm boot reliability remains a hardware acceptance requirement.

Upstream-Status: Pending

--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/bridge/lontium-lt9611.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/bridge/lontium-lt9611.c
@@ -486,7 +486,7 @@
 
 static int lt9611_power_on(struct lt9611 *lt9611)
 {
-	int ret;
+	int ret, attempt;
 	const struct reg_sequence seq[] = {
 		/* LT9611_System_Init */
 		{ 0x8101, 0x18 }, /* sel xtal clock */
@@ -515,9 +515,20 @@
 	if (lt9611->power_on)
 		return 0;
 
-	ret = regmap_multi_reg_write(lt9611->regmap, seq, ARRAY_SIZE(seq));
+	/* The i.MX adapter defaults to no arbitration-loss retries. */
+	for (attempt = 0; attempt < 3; attempt++) {
+		ret = regmap_multi_reg_write(lt9611->regmap, seq, ARRAY_SIZE(seq));
+		if (ret != -EAGAIN || attempt == 2)
+			break;
+
+		dev_dbg(lt9611->dev, "power-on arbitration loss, retry %d\n",
+			attempt + 1);
+		usleep_range(1000, 2000);
+	}
 	if (!ret)
 		lt9611->power_on = true;
+	if (!ret && attempt)
+		dev_info(lt9611->dev, "power-on recovered after %d retries\n", attempt);
 
 	return ret;
 }
